<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    ========================================================================
    PetNames_Ashkarr.xml         Jawa_Patches - authored 2026-08-23
    ========================================================================
    STAR_WARS_PET_NAMES_1, part 2 of 3. The corpus is
    Defs/RulePackDefs/Jawa_PetNames.xml; the Harmony hook that makes TAMING
    and BIRTH use it at all is in the JawaRules assembly.

    SCOPE, and why it is not "every animal". This repoints the ~320 ThingDefs
    that already carry SWAnimalNamerMale - Star Wars Animal Collection's own
    namer - and nothing else.
    ⛔ NOT the 1721 rows on NamerAnimalGenericMale. That would rename every
    animal on the planet including hostile fauna nobody ever tames, and a
    thumper called "Restocking Fee" charging the colony is not the joke.
    ⭐ Selecting BY THE EXISTING NAMER rather than by a def list means the set
    tracks the donor mod: an animal it adds later is covered automatically,
    and one it removes takes its own row with it.

    The donor's namer is Star Wars PERSON names - Aedalus, Ailyn, Amber - so
    there is no creature register and no humour register anywhere in the
    stack. That gap is the whole item.

    Both nameGenerator and nameGeneratorFemale point at ONE def: the corpus is
    deliberately unisex, and RaceProperties.GetNameGenerator falls back to
    nameGenerator when the female one is null anyway.

    ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing LOGS NOTHING. The Conditional here is a
    guard, not proof - the proof is the offline count in the item's verify,
    which reads the dump and checks SWAnimalNamerMale's row count dropped by
    exactly the number these gained.
    ========================================================================
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef/race/nameGenerator[text()="SWAnimalNamerMale"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef/race/nameGenerator[text()="SWAnimalNamerMale"]</xpath>
      <value><nameGenerator>Jawa_NamerPetSW</nameGenerator></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef/race/nameGeneratorFemale[text()="SWAnimalNamerFemale"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef/race/nameGeneratorFemale[text()="SWAnimalNamerFemale"]</xpath>
      <value><nameGeneratorFemale>Jawa_NamerPetSW</nameGeneratorFemale></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
